{title: From the Morning}
{artist: Nick Drake}

# Simplified ukulele arrangement (not the original guitar voicings)

# Chords: C (0003)  G (0232)  Am (2000)  F (2010)

# Suggested strum: Down, down-up, up-down-up (slow and gentle)

Verse 1
[C]A day once dawned, and it was [G]beautiful
[Am]A day once dawned from the [F]ground
[C]Then the night she [G]fell
[Am]And the air was [F]beautiful
[C]The night she [G]fell all a[C]round

Refrain
[F]So look, see the [C]days
The [G]endless coloured [Am]ways
[F]Go play the [G]game that you [C]learnt
From the [C]morning

Verse 2
[C]And now we [G]rise
[Am]And we are [F]everywhere
[C]And now we [G]rise from the [C]ground
[C]And see she [G]flies
[Am]She is [F]everywhere
[C]See she [G]flies all a[C]round

Refrain
[F]So look, see the [C]sights
The [G]endless summer [Am]nights
[F]And go play the [G]game that you [C]learnt
From the [C]mornin'

# Tip: Start with one gentle down-strum per chord, then add the strum pattern.
